Restart Tokri on the computer hosting the app

1. Open a terminal in this repository.
2. Stop the running app with Ctrl+C.
3. Pull the latest code and start the app:

   git pull --ff-only
   .venv/bin/python -m uvicorn app.main:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000 --reload

If Git reports conflicting local changes, preserve and resolve them before
continuing. Do not discard local work.

Keep the existing public tunnel running. On your other device, open the
public dashboard URL and refresh the page. If you restarted the tunnel,
use the new URL it prints.

Refreshing the browser does not pull new code from GitHub. The hosting
computer must pull the latest code first. Restart the app after backend
or .env changes.
